@format 1
@id logging.open-feed
@title Open log feed
@area 9. Logging
@entry input
@summary Load a selected log file into structured rows, apply category filtering, and append live entries in bounded batches.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related logging.emit-entry
@tag logging
@tag viewer

@alias logWindow = Cadroue.UIShell.PLogWindow
@alias traceWriter = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LTraceWriter

[input] Log window opens or file selection changes <input>
- Build available categories and log-file choices @ logWindow.PLogCategoryBuild(...)
- Select and request a log file @ logWindow.PLogFilesBuild(...)
> load

[load] Load selected log <process>
- Flush and read the selected log file @ traceWriter.LTraceFileRead(...)
- Parse the text into structured rows @ logWindow.PLogFileLoad(...)
- Limit retained rows and apply the selected category @ logWindow.PLogFileLoad(...)
> live

[live] Receive live entries <decision>
- Buffer trace notifications until the UI flush interval @ logWindow.PLogAppendHandle(...)
? "Selected file is the current live log" > append
? "A historical log is selected" > result

[append] Append visible batch <process>
- Add buffered entries to all rows, source text, and the filtered view @ logWindow.PLogFlushHandle(...)
- Enforce the row limit and scroll to the latest visible entry @ logWindow.PLogFlushHandle(...)
> result

[result] Log feed visible <output>
= The feed reflects the selected file and category, with live updates only for the current log.
